---
import PhotoSlot from './PhotoSlot.astro';
import config from '../config.json';
import { content, value, formatSince } from '../lib/content.ts';

// The join band used to sell: "Join Our Community / Connect with fellow math enthusiasts and join our
// monthly discussions", then a checklist — "Monthly in-person study sessions", "Collaborative
// problem-solving", "Network with math enthusiasts". Two of those were cadence claims in a section that had
// no source beside them, and all three were the template's words rather than the club's (the operator,
// 2026-11-03: "no humanity", "too professional"). They are on the retired list in
// `scripts/check-content.mjs`. What is here instead is the mechanics a stranger can actually use, each one
// read from `src/content.json` with its source: where meetings are held (`venues`), what the roster says and
// when it was read (`membership` — D136: the count is dated and has no '+' on it, and the regular-attendee
// figure is deliberately not published), and the two paths out.
const venues = value(content.venues);
const membership = value(content.membership);
const venueCount = Array.isArray(content.venues?.names) ? content.venues.names.length : null;
---

{/* `py-12` (48px): the band air is one ruled step across all four landing-page bands (R6, D214) — see the
    hero's note for what the trim bought and the reasons section's note for what it costs a row. */}
<section class="bg-paper py-12">
  <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-heading font-extrabold text-ink">
        Come once
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lede leading-prose text-ink-2 font-body max-w-measure mx-auto">
        One place to say you are coming, one place to argue. Neither takes a commitment, and one evening is
        enough to tell whether this is your kind of room.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 bg-panel rounded-card overflow-hidden">
      <div class="px-6 py-8 sm:p-10">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-subhead font-semibold text-ink mb-4">
              How it works
            </h3>
            <div class="space-y-3 text-body leading-prose text-ink-2 font-body">
              {venues && (
                <p>
                  {venues}
                  {venueCount ? ` The club has used ${venueCount} of them.` : ''} A date and its place go up
                  on Meetup; the discussion keeps running between meetings in the chat.
                </p>
              )}
              <p>
                Nobody hands you homework and there is no level to clear. If you would rather hear what is
                being argued about before you go, the chat invite is below.
              </p>
              {membership && (
                <p>
                  {membership} — counted {content.membership.asOf ? formatSince(content.membership.asOf) : 'today'},
                  and that is the list, not the room.
                </p>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- PS-3, the join media column (round 10 ruling: reserve it now). `npm run check:space` prints this
               column by its `data-slot` name — the survey ranks slot boxes by area, and a named box now rides
               along whatever its rank, because a floor that hides the only box the site labels makes every comment
               about that box unfalsifiable. Its box is **532x56 at 1240** (one paragraph) inside a grid row that is
               **326** tall; **310x85 at 390** and **240x113 at 320**, where the grid is one column.
               @measured 2026-11-03 by check:space
               What changed here on 2026-11-03: this column used to carry the two paths out, so its height WAS the
               call-to-action's height (532x128 at 1240, 310x245 at 390) and round 10 could call a plate here "a
               GROWTH of ~152px, not a reclamation". The actions now stand outside the card (see the note under the
               card), so the row's height belongs to the copy column beside it: at the reserved 532x128 the column
               becomes 128 + 32 + 56 = 216px against a 326px row, i.e. **0px of page height at 1240**. At 390 the
               same plate lands 310x75 and the column goes 85 -> 192, so there it is a **~107px growth**. That is
               arithmetic on measured parts, not a measured page delta — A3 re-measures it with `check:rhythm` once
               the plates are in.
               The call-to-action stays whether or not the plate does: art may add to the join path here, never
               replace it (D149-1b, D94). `data-slot` is a probe handle: `check:space` and `npm run round10`
               re-measure the applied box instead of trusting this comment. -->
          <div data-slot="PS-3">
          <PhotoSlot
            slot="join"
            ratio="532 / 128"
            caption="the club mid-session, wide crop (532x128)"
          />
          <p class="text-body leading-prose text-ink-2 font-body">
            The calendar and the sign-up live on Meetup. The chat is where the club decides what it is
            pulling on.
          </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- **The two paths out stand on the page's own ground, outside the tinted card.** Why here rather than in
         the card, in numbers: the secondary is `bg-paper inset-shadow-rule`, so its 1px ring has the control's
         own `paper` fill on one side and whatever the control stands on behind it on the other. Inside the card
         it stood on `panel`, and `--color-rule` measures **3.01 against paper, 2.88 against panel** — under the
         3.0 graphic bar on that side (design/records/0018-a-hairline-on-a-tint-is-under-its-own-bar.md). The
         operator's ruling (D149-3c, 2026-11-03) is that a keyline may not straddle two grounds and that the fix
         is the placement, not the number. `check:render` now measures both sides of every inset ring and fails
         the straddle, so the arrangement is gated rather than remembered.
         This is the same ruling as D141/D142 for a notice — an action belongs outside the boundary it is not a
         part of — and it has a product consequence worth naming: a photograph in PS-3 can now never displace
         the join path. The photo adds to the card; the paths out are the card's neighbours (DESIGN.md,
         "photo-free by construction"). -->
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        href={config.URLs.meetupGroup}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        data-control="primary"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 text-label font-semibold rounded-control text-band-text bg-ink hover:bg-ink-hover focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-gold transition"
      >
        Join on Meetup
        <svg class="ml-2 -mr-1 w-4 h-4" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
          <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10.293 3.293a1 1 0 011.414 0l6 6a1 1 0 010 1.414l-6 6a1 1 0 01-1.414-1.414L14.586 11H3a1 1 0 110-2h11.586l-4.293-4.293a1 1 0 010-1.414z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
        </svg>
      </a>
      <a
        href={config.URLs.discordInvite}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        data-control="secondary"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 text-label font-semibold rounded-control text-ink bg-paper inset-shadow-rule hover:bg-tint focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-gold transition"
      >
        Join the chat
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>